        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Tell Manufacturing LC2400 Series Heavy Duty Commercial  Leversets</b>\r\n<p>\r\nHeavy Duty Commercial  Leversets complies with ANSI/BHMA A156.4, Series 4000, Grade 2. Listed by UL / ULC for ratings of \u001cA\u001d  label (3 hours) and less, UL10C / UBC 7-2 (1997) positive pressure, for single doors up to 4\u0019'0\"\u001d x 8'\u00190\".  The chassis conforms to Grade 1 ANSI A156.2 specifications.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>These <a href=\"/pages/ada-compliant\"><b>ADA compliant levers</b></a> (conform to A117.1 Barrier Free Accessibility Code) are solid cast with a freewheeling clutch for added security and fully adjustable for 1-3/8\" to 2\" thick doors. \r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications </b> for Tell LC2400 Series Commercial Door Levers\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Door Thickness: Adjustable for 1-3/8\" to 2\" thick.</li>\r\n<li>Door Prep: Fits standard 161 door prep.</li>\r\n<li>Backsets: 2-3/4\" or 2-3/8\".</li>\r\n<li>Case: Steel mechanism. zinc dichromated plate for corrosion resistance.</li>\r\n<li>Chassis: Conforms to Grade 1 ANSI A156.2 specifications</li>\r\n<li>Clutch: Freewheeling clutch for added security</li>\r\n<li>Strike: 4-7/8\" X 1-1/4\" (Standard ASA Strike)</li>\r\n<li>Latchbolt: Stainless steel with 1/2\" throw. Deadlocking for keyed lock functions.</li>\r\n<li>Handing: Non-handed.</li>\r\n\r\n<li>Keyways: Schlage \"C\" Standard.</li>\r\n<li>Cylinder: Brass 6-pin cylinder keyed to 5-pins.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Available Functions </b> for for Tell LC2400 Series Commercial Door Levers\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Single Dummy: For use as a pull or to match trim, one (1) side.</li>\r\n<li>Passage (Hall or Closet): For doors that don't need locking.</li>\r\n<li>Privacy (Bedroom or Bathroom): For doors that could need locking.</li>\r\n<li>Keyed Entry: Outside lever locked by key. Push and turn button locking inside. When outside lever locked by push and turn button inside, key from outside or rotating inside lever retracts latch and does not unlock outside lever.</li>\r\n<li>Office: Outside lever locked and unlocked by key. Push button locking inside. When outside lever is locked, operating key in outside lever or operating inside lever unlocks push button and retracts latch.</li>\r\n<li>Classroom. Outside lever locked and unlocked by key. Inside lever always  unlocked</li>\r\n<li>Storeroom: Outside lever fixed. Entry by key only. Inside lever always unlocked. </li>\r\n<li>Communicating: Latchbolt operated by lever one side at all times. This is a single lever, maybe used inside or outside. </li>\r\n\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>",
